Real-World Applications

This challenge is a great introduction to steganography, the practice of hiding data in seemingly normal files. In cybersecurity, similar techniques are used in malware obfuscation, watermarking, and covert communications. Understanding how data can be hidden in plain sight is crucial for digital forensics and security analysis.

This kind of analysis is commonly used in:

    Malware analysis: Detecting hidden payloads in seemingly harmless files.
    Data leakage detection: Uncovering hidden messages in documents.
    Cyber forensics: Recovering deleted or hidden evidence from suspect files.
    
    
